{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1766297,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Space and beyond: Ideathon 2026","festival_id":null,"organization_id":437306,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-05T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-16T00:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"hackathons","public_url":"hackathons\/space-and-beyond-ideathon-2026-netaji-subhash-university-of-technology-main-campus-1766297","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Space &amp; Beyond &ndash; Innovation Ideathon 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>About the Event<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Space &amp; Beyond &ndash; Innovation Ideathon 2026 is an idea-based innovation challenge where participants will identify real-world problems and propose creative, practical, and impactful solutions.<\/p>\n<p>Participants can choose any one of the following themes:<\/p>\n<p><strong>Beyond Earth<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Ideas related to space exploration, future habitats, satellites, space technology, life beyond Earth, and the future of humanity in space.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Smart World, Better Future<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Ideas that use technology and innovation to solve real-world problems and improve everyday life.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Future without Limits<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Open-ended innovative ideas that address future challenges and create new possibilities.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Participation Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants can participate individually or in teams of 2&ndash;4 members.<\/li>\n<li>A participant can be a member of only one team.<\/li>\n<li>The event is open to eligible college students.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must submit one original idea.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Event Structure<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Round 1 &ndash; Registration and Ppt Submission<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must register for the Ideathon.<\/li>\n<li>Each team must submit one PPT presenting their proposed idea.<\/li>\n<li>The PPT should contain a maximum of 8&ndash;10 slides.<\/li>\n<li>The idea should clearly explain the problem, proposed solution, innovation, implementation, feasibility, impact, and future scope.<\/li>\n<li>Based on the submitted ideas, selected teams will qualify for Round 2.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Last Date for Registration and Ppt Submission: 15 October 2026<\/p>\n<p><strong>Round 1 Results: 16 October 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Round 2 &ndash; Prototype and Final Presentation<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shortlisted teams will develop a prototype based on their Round 1 idea.<\/li>\n<li>Participants can use Figma or any other suitable prototyping tool.<\/li>\n<li>The prototype should demonstrate the key features, working concept, or user flow of the proposed solution.<\/li>\n<li>A fully functional product is not mandatory. A well-designed prototype or mock-up is sufficient.<\/li>\n<li>Teams must prepare a PPT to explain their solution and prototype.<\/li>\n<li>Teams will present their prototype and PPT before the judging panel.<\/li>\n<li>Judges may ask questions regarding the idea, prototype, implementation, feasibility, and future scope.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Prototype and Final Ppt Presentation: 18 October 2026<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Ppt Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximum 8&ndash;10 slides.<\/li>\n<li>Keep the presentation clear, concise, and visually appealing.<\/li>\n<li>Use diagrams, flowcharts, images, and visuals wherever appropriate.<\/li>\n<li>Avoid excessive text.<\/li>\n<li>The content and idea should be original or properly credited.<\/li>\n<li>The PPT should be submitted in PPTX or PDF format as specified by the organizers.<\/li>\n<li>Suggested file name: TeamName_SpaceAndBeyond<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Suggested Ppt Structure<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Title and Team Details<\/li>\n<li>Problem Statement<\/li>\n<li>Proposed Solution<\/li>\n<li>Innovation and Uniqueness<\/li>\n<li>Working or Implementation<\/li>\n<li>Technology or Resources Required<\/li>\n<li>Feasibility and Scalability<\/li>\n<li>Expected Impact<\/li>\n<li>Future Scope<\/li>\n<li>Conclusion<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Prototype Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The prototype must be based on the idea submitted in Round 1.<\/li>\n<li>Participants may use Figma or any other suitable prototyping tool.<\/li>\n<li>The prototype should demonstrate the main features and user flow of the proposed solution.<\/li>\n<li>A fully functional product is not required.<\/li>\n<li>A clickable or mock-up prototype is acceptable.<\/li>\n<li>Teams should be able to explain how the prototype can be developed into a real-world solution.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":762485,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-05T21:39:10+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T00:07:55+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"online_coding_challenge","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"5mKA9Iv","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":2,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":15,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-10-05 21:43:17","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":true,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6ac3cbc394d5a_1000105080.png","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/150x150\/uploadedManual-6ac3cbc394d5a_1000105080.png","regnRequirements":{"id":2497965,"opport